   "text": "A curve $C$ is defined for $x > 0$. At every point $(x, y)$ on $C$,\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} = 3\\sqrt{x} + \\frac{32}{x^3} - 2.$$\nThe point $(4, 10)$ lies on $C$.\n\nFind an equation for $C$, giving $y$ in terms of $x$ with each term in its simplest form. (5)",
